;; Graph-level recursion primitive.
;;
;; The cycle constraints (per-binding + sync-time topological-sort)
;; reject every self/mutual ref in the fn-graph. Without escape, a
;; recursive fn-def is structurally impossible to write — admins
;; either fall back to `exec/execute-by-name` from inside a base-fn
;; impl (violates Code = Graph) or open-code the recursion in
;; Clojure (defeats the editor / type-checker / layout).
;;
;; `:fix` provides the escape WITHOUT relaxing the cycle invariant
;; — it synthesises a self-referential callable at runtime from a
;; step fn that receives `:self` as a call-site arg. Recursion is
;; expressed as: "step receives self + input; the body decides
;; whether to recurse (`:invoke :func :self :arg <next>`) or
;; terminate." No graph-level cycle is required; the recursive
;; structure is created when `:fix`'s impl wires `:self` to the
;; step's own invocation.
;;
;; Recursion depth is bounded by `*max-recursion-depth*` (default
;; 1000; configurable per call via `binding`). A runaway step that
;; never hits its base case throws `:recursion-error/max-depth-
;; exceeded` instead of blowing the JVM stack.

{:namespace "core.recursion"
 :description "Graph-level recursion via Y-combinator-style :fix primitive — step fn receives :self as a call-site arg, depth-bounded by `*max-recursion-depth*`."
 :fns
 [{:name :fix
   :description "Y-combinator-style recursion primitive. Invokes `:step` with `{:input <initial> :self <recursive-callable>}`; `:step` returns either a terminal value OR recurses by invoking `:self` with the next input (`:invoke :func :self :arg <next>`). Bounded by `*max-recursion-depth*` (default 1000)."
   :args {:step {:type [:fn {:input :any :self [:fn {:arg :any} :any]} :any]
                 :description "Step fn. Receives `:input` (the current iteration's value) and `:self` (a 1-arg callable that re-enters the step with a new input). MUST have a base case that does NOT invoke `:self`."}
          :input {:type :any
                  :description "Initial value passed to the first invocation of `:step`."}}
   :return-type :any
   :effects #{}}]}
